===Verb===
{{en-verb|pay<,,paid> through the nose}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[pay#Verb|pay]] an [[exorbitant]] or [[excessive]] [[amount#Noun|amount]], either in [[money#Noun|money]] or in some other [[manner#Noun|manner]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{hypernyms|en|pay over the odds}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1650|author=G[eorge] W[alker]|title=Anglo-tyrannus, or The Idea of a Norman Monarch, Represented in the Paralell Reignes of Henrie the Third and Charles Kings of England,{{nb...|wherein the Whole Management of Affairs under the Norman Kings is Manifested, together with the Real Ground, and Rise of All those Former, and these Latter Contestations between the Princes, and People of this Nation, upon the Score of Prerogative and Liberty. And the Impious, Abusive, and Delusive Practises are in Short Discovered, by which the English have been Bobbed of their Freedome, and the Norman Tyrannie Founded and Continued over Them.}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415125916/https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/eebo/A96861.0001.001?rgn=main;view=fulltext|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} George Thompson{{nb...|at the signe of the White Horse in Chancery Lane}}|page=20|pageurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415125916/https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/eebo/A96861.0001.001/28?vid=110807|oclc=84199215|passage=Observe here the happy estate of our Ancestors under Monarchy, who, if they gained but this advantage {{...}} of receiving a few good Grants, and enjoying a pittance of Freedom, once in 4 or 5 ages when their King was too young to play ''Rex,'' and there hapned a wise and honest Protector; yet were sure to '''pay through the nose''' for it afterwards with double and treble interest for forbearance.}}
#* {{RQ:Marvell Rehearsal|page=270|passage=But vvhen they came to ſeek for Match, and Bullet, and Povvder, there vvas none to be had. The Fanaticks had bought it all up, and made them '''pay''' for it moſt unconſcionably, and '''through the noſe'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Lesage Smollett Gil Blas|edition=3rd|volume=I|chapter=Gil Blas Acquires the Theatrical Taste, Abandons Himself to the Pleasures of a Comic Life, with which however, He is Disgusted in a Little Time|page=257|passage=[F]armers of the revenue vvere admitted, vvho, far from being gratified for their preſence, as they are in their ovvn aſſemblies, vvere obliged to '''pay through the noſe''' for their reception.}}
#* {{RQ:Burney Cecilia|volume=V|chapter=A Prating|page=287|passage=[S]he {{quote-gloss|a lady}}'s a mere nobody, as one may ſay, till ſhe can get herſelf a huſband, being ſhe knovvs nothing of buſineſs, and is made to '''pay''' for every thing '''through the noſe'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1795|month=December|title=[Monthly Chronicle. Home News.] Hare and Stag Chace.|journal=The Freemasons’ Magazine: Or, General and Complete Library|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for the proprietor, & sold by}} J. Parsons,{{nb...|No. 21, Paternoster Row, & all booksellers in town & country.}}|volume=V|page=433|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1AkOAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA433|oclc=1264849997|passage=Several persons have already left off ''snuff-taking'', in consequence of the additional duty on tobacco, observing that they have no idea of '''''paying through the nose''''' for the expence of war.}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Osbourne Wrong Box|chapter=Final Adjustment of the Leather Business|page=282|passage=I seem to understand that this gentleman {{...}} is the ''fons et origo'' of the trouble; and, from what I gather, he has already '''paid through the nose'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Kyne Valley|chapter=XXXVI|page=358|passage="You'll '''pay through the nose''' for this, you scoundrel," Sexton whimpered. "I'll fix you, you traitor."}}
#* {{RQ:Galsworthy In Chancery|chapter=Where Forsytes Fear to Tread|page=159|passage=[T]hat fellow would milk the settlements somehow, and make his family '''pay through the nose''' to keep him out of bankruptcy or perhaps even gaol!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=w:Francine Mathews|chapter=1|title=Death in Rough Water|series=A Merry Folger Mystery|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:William Morrow and Company|page=12|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/deathinroughwate00math/page/12/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-688-13473-0|passage=Somebody figured out that a harpooned fish dies quicker and tastes better than one caught by the long-liners' nets. Whole Foods '''pays through the nose''' for it, all over the country. So do restaurants.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=8 April 2021|title=Brace for the Amazon effect on live sport|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210408155547/https://www.economist.com/business/2021/04/08/brace-for-the-amazon-effect-on-live-sport|passage=At a time when other entertainment is available at a sliver of the price from Netflix and other streaming services, live sport is the only thing left to induce viewers to '''pay through the nose''' for pay-TV.}}

